1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,440
Itchy? Itchy, Sosu. Sosu. Itchy, Sosu.

2
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:20,200
Uh, hey, Fapta? Are you really sure that your wounds are feeling okay? They look pretty bad.

3
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:27,140
Hadi, no need to worry. Fapta cannot be hurt. Edge part is fine, Sosu.

4
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:34,180
Um, there's more to it than just the edge. Oh, Rag, are you worrying about Fapta?

5
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:41,020
Well, of course. You're injured. Again? Pet me again? Like before, around the horns like I like?

6
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:52,640
Here? I'm not touching your wound, right? Harder. Scratch me a little harder, Sosu.

7
00:00:52,640 --> 00:01:01,780
Hey, uh, Fapta? So why are you doing all this for me anyway?

8
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:05,960
Hey, uh, Fapta?

9
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:13,840
What's wrong?

10
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:17,500
All the beasts going crazy over the smell of Fapta's blood.

11
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:20,100
Mayan!

12
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:23,940
We leave that to Gabaroon and go, Sosu.

13
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:29,760
Padding is precious, Sosu. But freshness is more important.

14
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:37,740
Rake's back!

15
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,900
Rake! I'm so glad you're okay!

16
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:49,520
Um, uh, uh, hey, um, what's that?

17
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:54,260
I can explain it to you later. The blood is attracting a lot of bugs and stuff.

18
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:55,680
Let's get inside.

19
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:56,680
Uh...

20
00:01:56,680 --> 00:02:00,640
Uh, huh?

21
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:06,960
Fapta?

22
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:10,140
Riko?

23
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:12,060
Uh, uh-huh.

24
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:14,180
Come on, Minya.

25
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:15,580
Uh, uh!

26
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:36,420
Uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh, uh...

27
00:03:58,029 --> 00:04:14,909
What? Is that from the princess? I heard she was immortal, but that seems... I... I just... I guess I had no idea.

28
00:04:17,789 --> 00:04:20,149
This is... This must be the balancing.

29
00:04:20,509 --> 00:04:26,529
Similar, but strange. All of Iru Buru is trying out. This is a first for Katja.

30
00:04:26,529 --> 00:04:29,489
Reg, it must be because we have part of Falfta here.

31
00:04:29,889 --> 00:04:35,549
Hey, what should I do with this? Do you think we should bring it to where Nanachi is?

32
00:04:36,289 --> 00:04:40,669
Wait, well, you... you can't just take it the way it looks right now.

33
00:04:41,309 --> 00:04:49,089
The one who bought your friend? Well, if you show it to him, I think... that would probably make him break.

34
00:04:49,449 --> 00:04:49,789
Huh?

35
00:04:50,649 --> 00:04:54,329
And if he does, I don't know what'll happen to your friend in there.

36
00:04:54,329 --> 00:04:59,949
And... um... sorry. How exactly did you get that?

37
00:05:01,109 --> 00:05:06,129
So long as I keep my promise. She said she'd give anything and gave... this.

38
00:05:06,329 --> 00:05:08,369
What kind of... a promise?

39
00:05:08,369 --> 00:05:14,149
You want me... to... destroy the village?

40
00:05:15,149 --> 00:05:17,489
Falfta wants to, but not possible.

41
00:05:18,189 --> 00:05:20,689
Reg is too kind, so cannot do it, Sosu.

42
00:05:20,969 --> 00:05:21,269
Hadi.

43
00:05:22,329 --> 00:05:26,009
So Falfta need Reg help to get inside, so Reg no have to.

44
00:05:26,429 --> 00:05:29,969
Make it so Falfta can go inside of Mother without trouble.

45
00:05:29,969 --> 00:05:37,369
Reg, you said comes out of hand. You said Tufapta can rewrite Sosu.

46
00:05:37,889 --> 00:05:41,509
But you... you said couldn't use because leaving to search for Haku.

47
00:05:41,969 --> 00:05:44,849
You said next time see Fapta will take me with you.

48
00:05:45,189 --> 00:05:47,669
You said you take Fapta to where they are.

49
00:05:48,249 --> 00:05:49,489
And to Mother...

50
00:05:49,489 --> 00:05:50,369
Hey, now wait!

51
00:05:50,489 --> 00:05:52,709
...want you to take me inside, Chosu.

52
00:05:52,709 --> 00:05:54,069
Hold it! Why are you biting?

53
00:05:54,489 --> 00:05:58,889
Reg, you say if Ken rewrite, you change laws not letting Falfta through.

54
00:05:59,309 --> 00:06:00,909
You do that inside, Sosu.

55
00:06:01,509 --> 00:06:02,409
The incinerator!

56
00:06:02,869 --> 00:06:05,709
It's powerful enough to rewrite the rules of the netherworld.

57
00:06:06,089 --> 00:06:07,429
That's what Nanachi said.

58
00:06:07,809 --> 00:06:08,869
What is it?

59
00:06:09,269 --> 00:06:10,829
Reg can shoot it from his hands!

60
00:06:11,069 --> 00:06:12,269
It can burn up anything!

61
00:06:12,689 --> 00:06:17,509
Falfta told me a long time ago, I said it's possible to tear a hole in the wall.

62
00:06:18,009 --> 00:06:19,269
Well, well...

63
00:06:20,269 --> 00:06:22,049
You were the prince all along.

64
00:06:22,709 --> 00:06:26,069
And to think you actually brought back a piece of the princess!

65
00:06:26,949 --> 00:06:31,829
Seems the village has been thrown into chaos by this new value, which shouldn't even exist.

66
00:06:32,429 --> 00:06:34,669
Oh, Vueko, that looks good on you.

67
00:06:35,069 --> 00:06:37,649
But that thing on your head is actually underwear.

68
00:06:37,829 --> 00:06:39,469
It's for villagers with lots of legs.

69
00:06:42,069 --> 00:06:45,909
The shopkeeper said it could also be used as a hood.

70
00:06:46,749 --> 00:06:48,929
So, you finally came out, huh?

71
00:06:49,229 --> 00:06:50,669
Good. I'm so glad.

72
00:06:50,669 --> 00:06:53,949
I take it you already told these kids about the princess.

73
00:06:53,949 --> 00:06:55,009
I did.

74
00:06:55,449 --> 00:06:57,809
I centered the story on myself, though.

75
00:06:57,809 --> 00:06:58,949
I see.

76
00:06:59,609 --> 00:07:00,089
Riko.

77
00:07:00,089 --> 00:07:03,229
So, do you hate me now?

78
00:07:04,229 --> 00:07:06,669
I don't really know you yet to decide that.

79
00:07:07,149 --> 00:07:09,129
But I do like this village.

80
00:07:10,009 --> 00:07:12,149
After all, there's lots of others like me here.

81
00:07:12,709 --> 00:07:15,329
Even more than when I was an orc living with my own people.

82
00:07:15,329 --> 00:07:17,949
Oh? And how are they like you?

83
00:07:18,469 --> 00:07:19,129
Let's see.

84
00:07:19,829 --> 00:07:20,729
I guess...

85
00:07:20,729 --> 00:07:26,369
Well, Wazukyan, I have to wonder, did you descend this far even knowing you were going past the point of no return?

86
00:07:26,709 --> 00:07:27,149
Yeah.

87
00:07:27,709 --> 00:07:30,469
I mean, that was the kind of trip we were on.

88
00:07:30,469 --> 00:07:34,069
Oh, I see. That's what you're getting at.

89
00:07:34,749 --> 00:07:36,769
I heard from the Sovereign of Dawn.

90
00:07:37,069 --> 00:07:38,629
You know him, right? Bondrewd?

91
00:07:39,009 --> 00:07:43,049
He said that even you cave raiders who made their living in this giant pit,

92
00:07:43,529 --> 00:07:47,849
there's only a handful of humans who will descend to a depth that's impossible to return from.

93
00:07:48,149 --> 00:07:49,309
And you're one of them.

94
00:07:49,309 --> 00:07:55,949
One who, while searching for their own gold, found that the place where the darkness lies is even more valuable.

95
00:07:56,449 --> 00:08:02,289
One whose home is found only in the continuation of their quest, and who could only choose to push forward.

96
00:08:02,809 --> 00:08:07,089
This place is a sanctuary for such types who have nowhere left to go.

97
00:08:07,749 --> 00:08:12,449
And let me tell you, there's not a single villager here who wouldn't do the same thing.

98
00:08:12,969 --> 00:08:13,409
Hadi.

99
00:08:13,409 --> 00:08:22,149
Well, yeah. I found tons of value after ending up here, but my days of challenging the pit harken back to my longing.

100
00:08:22,909 --> 00:08:26,189
There's hardly been a day I don't dream of such things.

101
00:08:26,729 --> 00:08:27,209
Hadi.

102
00:08:28,549 --> 00:08:30,129
Oh, you okay, Riko?

103
00:08:30,669 --> 00:08:32,129
I wonder why that is.

104
00:08:32,949 --> 00:08:36,129
Hey, um, Wazukyan? So I, uh, I'm sorry.

105
00:08:36,609 --> 00:08:41,129
I said I don't really know you yet, but actually, there is one thing I know about you.

106
00:08:41,129 --> 00:08:46,289
No matter what you had to sacrifice or trample over, you wanted your wish to come true.

107
00:08:47,129 --> 00:08:51,989
This village where you stay, the creation of this homeland for those who have nowhere to go,

108
00:08:52,249 --> 00:08:54,329
I don't believe that was truly your wish.

109
00:08:55,469 --> 00:09:01,229
If the golden city you saw really does exist in the Abyss, the sixth layer is still only the entrance.

110
00:09:02,229 --> 00:09:08,089
There's no way you, someone who finds value in that extraordinary quest, would choose to stop at the entrance.

111
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:12,209
So why? Why are you pretending you've given up on your adventure?

112
00:09:13,129 --> 00:09:19,489
Interesting. In the roughly 150 years since the creation of this village, you're the first to notice.

113
00:09:20,269 --> 00:09:23,489
Still, like the others, I can't leave this place.

114
00:09:24,389 --> 00:09:28,669
We can only live within the boundary. Things don't always work out, you know.

115
00:09:28,669 --> 00:09:32,869
What's the matter, Riko?

116
00:09:33,709 --> 00:09:41,389
Fopta has the wish-granting power of all three Cradles of Desire, the only ones who can use the power of the Cradles.

117
00:09:41,969 --> 00:09:47,249
Um, hey, Wazukyan, could it be that you want me to use the power of the Cradles of Desire?

118
00:09:47,829 --> 00:09:51,229
To make it so that the villagers can go back to adventuring again?

119
00:09:51,229 --> 00:09:58,009
Hmm. How did you come to that conclusion?

120
00:09:59,329 --> 00:10:05,269
I've had something like that happen. Besides, I heard you're someone who does everything he can.

121
00:10:06,529 --> 00:10:08,149
Yes, that's great!

122
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:11,889
Oh, wow, really? You're... you're not denying it?

123
00:10:12,529 --> 00:10:12,849
Hmm?

124
00:10:13,689 --> 00:10:18,389
Challenging the Abyss again. I've dreamed of that scenario countless times.

125
00:10:18,949 --> 00:10:21,689
But it's not something you should burden someone with.

126
00:10:22,129 --> 00:10:28,049
It's not like that, Mugi. I'm not the one who will choose. These kids will, ultimately.

127
00:10:28,809 --> 00:10:32,329
The choice can only be made by the challengers.

128
00:10:33,829 --> 00:10:34,869
That rumbling.

129
00:10:34,869 --> 00:10:48,989
Now, Riko, Reg, what will you choose?

130
00:10:48,989 --> 00:10:50,989
That's...

131
00:10:50,989 --> 00:11:10,369
That's Chiroemo.

132
00:11:10,849 --> 00:11:11,689
Yeah, Chiroemo!

133
00:11:12,229 --> 00:11:15,829
Damn it. I knew it. Bastard was just buying time.

134
00:11:15,829 --> 00:11:19,829
Hey, boy. That thing has come for the piece of the princess you're holding.

135
00:11:23,409 --> 00:11:24,869
You're coming with me.

136
00:11:28,069 --> 00:11:31,749
I'll distract it! Riko! Head somewhere safe!

137
00:11:32,529 --> 00:11:33,209
Reg!

138
00:11:33,749 --> 00:11:36,029
Ma! I need you to take care of Riko!

139
00:11:36,829 --> 00:11:43,469
Yes! It's turning this way!

140
00:11:43,469 --> 00:11:53,129
Good! It's not very fast! I can outrun it!

141
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:55,189
But what should I do?

142
00:11:57,889 --> 00:12:00,469
What? Something slimy is...

143
00:12:00,469 --> 00:12:03,029
Look, it's starting now.

144
00:12:03,289 --> 00:12:05,189
W-Why'd you bring me back here?

145
00:12:05,649 --> 00:12:05,929
Hmm?

146
00:12:05,929 --> 00:12:08,569
Because you're quick to give in to despair.

147
00:12:09,289 --> 00:12:11,209
Just stay here and watch.

148
00:12:11,449 --> 00:12:13,389
There's something I want to know.

149
00:12:14,109 --> 00:12:15,589
Or actually...

150
00:12:15,589 --> 00:12:17,429
Want some confirmation on.

151
00:12:17,589 --> 00:12:18,209
What is it?

152
00:12:18,629 --> 00:12:19,709
That huge thing.

153
00:12:20,389 --> 00:12:24,049
Why does it have the same name as the piece of trash you took me in?

154
00:12:24,049 --> 00:12:25,169
Jiroemo?

155
00:12:26,529 --> 00:12:29,349
Iremui made him from signals she received from you.

156
00:12:29,729 --> 00:12:30,889
You're special to her.

157
00:12:31,909 --> 00:12:33,889
Iremui was extremely lonely.

158
00:12:34,609 --> 00:12:36,789
After all, you just kept on brooding.

159
00:12:37,789 --> 00:12:41,989
So one day, he just appeared and said he was one of the three sages.

160
00:12:43,349 --> 00:12:45,029
He can talk.

161
00:12:45,029 --> 00:12:50,949
When the village is in danger, he comes to take out the threat, like some sort of guardian.

162
00:12:51,609 --> 00:12:56,109
But if he gets that piece of fakta, then he's doomed.

163
00:12:56,369 --> 00:13:01,049
Because no matter how big he is, he won't come out of the balance and unscathed.

164
00:13:01,409 --> 00:13:04,469
I told you, he's connected to you.

165
00:13:05,469 --> 00:13:09,229
Rather than being a hollow, he's more like a part of this place.

166
00:13:09,229 --> 00:13:11,729
That thing is the will of the village.

167
00:13:12,549 --> 00:13:13,709
What the...

168
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:15,189
What's happening to it?

169
00:13:15,549 --> 00:13:16,069
Balancing?

170
00:13:16,629 --> 00:13:18,229
No, it looks like...

171
00:13:18,769 --> 00:13:21,909
It became one with the slimy stuff?

172
00:13:25,809 --> 00:13:27,349
The entrance to the village!

173
00:13:27,689 --> 00:13:28,229
Very good!

174
00:13:28,989 --> 00:13:31,529
You're not gonna let those kids get away, are you?

175
00:13:39,229 --> 00:13:43,989
Something...

176
00:13:43,989 --> 00:13:44,709
Oh, no.

177
00:13:55,709 --> 00:13:55,989
Huh?

178
00:14:05,549 --> 00:14:06,909
The wall is...

179
00:14:06,909 --> 00:14:08,309
The wall's getting buried!

180
00:14:08,309 --> 00:14:11,089
I don't have nowhere left to run!

181
00:14:12,969 --> 00:14:19,209
Okay, since fakta is the embodiment of value, if I let it have some of this, will the balancing stop that thing?

182
00:14:19,429 --> 00:14:20,489
He's wavering.

183
00:14:20,889 --> 00:14:22,769
Being indecisive, that's great!

184
00:14:24,449 --> 00:14:25,549
Listen, boy!

185
00:14:26,669 --> 00:14:29,289
That thing's creation, give back to me!

186
00:14:29,669 --> 00:14:31,369
The balancing won't affect him!

187
00:14:32,369 --> 00:14:35,509
A piece of the princess won't stop him from what he's doing!

188
00:14:35,509 --> 00:14:36,929
He's decided!

189
00:14:37,409 --> 00:14:39,649
You're in danger and we'll try to consume you!

190
00:14:39,849 --> 00:14:41,029
You must run!

191
00:14:41,889 --> 00:14:42,509
Vueco...

192
00:14:43,089 --> 00:14:43,529
Run!

193
00:14:45,189 --> 00:14:46,069
You okay?

194
00:14:46,389 --> 00:14:48,809
That's the first time I've seen you shout like that.

195
00:14:50,089 --> 00:14:50,689
My...

196
00:14:50,689 --> 00:14:52,209
My voice was the one thing.

197
00:14:52,629 --> 00:14:54,089
I had plenty of time to train.

198
00:14:54,089 --> 00:14:56,869
I know you told me to run, but...

199
00:14:56,869 --> 00:14:58,049
But where can I go?

200
00:15:06,929 --> 00:15:08,869
A thin, slimy...

201
00:15:08,869 --> 00:15:10,129
Film?

202
00:15:10,129 --> 00:15:20,589
Whoa, is he trying to cover the entire village?

203
00:15:21,329 --> 00:15:23,169
This is looking bad.

204
00:15:26,969 --> 00:15:28,329
Don't touch it hard!

205
00:15:28,549 --> 00:15:29,049
Vueco!

206
00:15:29,589 --> 00:15:30,389
Oh, crap!

207
00:15:30,749 --> 00:15:32,709
He doesn't care if it gets the villagers too?

208
00:15:32,709 --> 00:15:41,309
Stop it!

209
00:15:41,889 --> 00:15:42,749
No, don't!

210
00:15:43,449 --> 00:15:44,909
No, don't you need that!

211
00:15:44,909 --> 00:15:45,309
No!

212
00:15:45,309 --> 00:15:59,289
I have to do it, don't I?

213
00:15:59,849 --> 00:16:02,729
Fakta will offer everything before our promise.

214
00:16:02,949 --> 00:16:04,309
Fakta will do it, Sosu.

215
00:16:04,989 --> 00:16:07,329
But I do like this village.

216
00:16:07,789 --> 00:16:09,029
That village is Mother.

217
00:16:09,309 --> 00:16:12,449
She fell into despair so deep she lost her voice, Sosu.

218
00:16:12,449 --> 00:16:16,349
Mother's regret, Mother's anger.

219
00:16:16,849 --> 00:16:18,689
Those things must be dispelled.

220
00:16:20,069 --> 00:16:22,969
I don't have the power to change things all on my own.

221
00:16:25,209 --> 00:16:27,689
Okay, there's no one behind him.

222
00:16:28,409 --> 00:16:29,569
It's a clear shot.

223
00:16:30,249 --> 00:16:32,789
From this angle, I'd hit him for sure.

224
00:16:36,109 --> 00:16:39,169
But can doing this really change things for the better?

225
00:16:39,709 --> 00:16:40,329
I don't know.

226
00:16:40,329 --> 00:16:43,369
Well, at this point...

227
00:16:43,369 --> 00:16:46,329
Now, there's no time to hesitate!

228
00:16:46,329 --> 00:16:46,569
Wait!

229
00:17:16,329 --> 00:17:26,689
I... I'm sorry. I couldn't think of any other way.

230
00:17:27,429 --> 00:17:28,949
Fakta is coming, and soon!

231
00:17:29,409 --> 00:17:31,209
I fear things are going to get really bad.

232
00:17:31,629 --> 00:17:33,629
Now until I wake back up after fainting,

233
00:17:33,889 --> 00:17:36,789
find somewhere as safe as you possibly can to hide from her!

234
00:17:36,809 --> 00:17:37,569
After you faint?

235
00:17:37,949 --> 00:17:39,269
Yeah, it's the incinerator.

236
00:17:39,629 --> 00:17:41,169
I pass out after using it.

237
00:17:41,169 --> 00:17:43,829
I still have some time left, a few minutes.

238
00:17:43,829 --> 00:17:46,569
But soon, drowsiness will wash over me.

239
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:48,889
Can I offer this for a favor?

240
00:17:50,089 --> 00:17:53,649
Until I wake up, will you please keep Riko safe inside?

241
00:17:54,069 --> 00:17:56,169
Because outside is the Abyss's world.

242
00:17:56,629 --> 00:17:59,769
I'm sure you know, but it's far more dangerous out there.

243
00:18:00,469 --> 00:18:00,909
Please!

244
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:04,709
Of course we'll do what you ask. We would be honored.

245
00:18:04,949 --> 00:18:07,749
But that's a tall order for just us three to pull off.

246
00:18:07,749 --> 00:18:09,809
Oh, Kaja will get more help.

247
00:18:13,829 --> 00:18:35,289
Aduh!

248
00:18:35,289 --> 00:18:49,289
Stand back. You are in the presence of a princess.

249
00:18:49,289 --> 00:18:52,289
Sosu. Reg, you have my thanks.

250
00:18:52,289 --> 00:18:56,289
But Fopta will not forgive villagers.

251
00:18:56,289 --> 00:19:01,289
My siblings and Fopta. You glared at us with hungry eyes.

252
00:19:01,289 --> 00:19:05,289
Fopta will not forgive those eyes, your mouths.

253
00:19:05,289 --> 00:19:09,289
You speak in the same tongue my mother did and spit out prayers.

254
00:19:09,289 --> 00:19:12,289
Fopta will not forgive those mouths.

255
00:19:12,289 --> 00:19:14,289
Fopta will not forgive your forms.

256
00:19:14,289 --> 00:19:18,289
You desecrated my mother to selfishly save your own skins.

257
00:19:18,289 --> 00:19:23,289
Fopta will not forgive your lives, which have continued for too long.

258
00:19:23,289 --> 00:19:28,289
Fopta will not forgive your wishes, your joy, your sorrow, your passions.

259
00:19:28,289 --> 00:19:31,289
Fopta will not let any of that continue.

260
00:19:31,289 --> 00:19:37,289
Fopta will never forgive your existence until you are dust, scraped and disregarded.

261
00:19:37,289 --> 00:19:41,289
Fopta was born, so this will not be forgotten.

262
00:19:41,289 --> 00:19:45,289
You know not how Fopta has longed for this day.

263
00:19:45,289 --> 00:19:48,289
Fopta will allow you no time to prepare.

264
00:19:48,289 --> 00:19:51,289
Fopta will eradicate you.

265
00:19:51,289 --> 00:20:00,289
Do not interfere, Sosu.

266
00:20:00,289 --> 00:20:10,289
Brothers and sisters, your youngest sibling has now returned home, Sosu.

267
00:20:10,289 --> 00:20:14,289
You did a good job supporting mother.

268
00:20:14,289 --> 00:20:15,289
You've done enough.

269
00:20:15,289 --> 00:20:17,289
She's all healed.

270
00:20:17,289 --> 00:20:19,289
It is none other than the immortal princess.

271
00:20:19,289 --> 00:20:21,289
What should Kaja do?

272
00:20:21,289 --> 00:20:22,289
So happy.

273
00:20:22,289 --> 00:20:35,289
And so it begins.

274
00:20:35,289 --> 00:20:41,289
And so it begins.

275
00:20:41,289 --> 00:21:08,289
Nah, who's singing?

276
00:21:08,289 --> 00:21:09,289
Miri.

277
00:21:09,289 --> 00:21:12,289
Just now, I was having a strange dream.

278
00:21:12,289 --> 00:21:21,289
And in it, there was a man who seemed like a friend, and I felt I needed him to survive.

279
00:21:21,289 --> 00:21:27,289
I was going along with him on some kind of search.

280
00:21:27,289 --> 00:21:32,289
I, I can't remember what we were looking for.

281
00:21:32,289 --> 00:21:37,289
The people he was with sorta resembled us.

282
00:21:37,289 --> 00:21:41,289
Even though, they didn't really look like us at all.

283
00:21:41,289 --> 00:21:46,289
Eventually, they finally found it.

284
00:21:46,289 --> 00:21:48,289
Their treasure.

285
00:21:48,289 --> 00:21:53,289
And for some reason, I couldn't look away.

286
00:21:53,289 --> 00:21:58,289
I don't know why, but it...

287
00:21:58,289 --> 00:22:02,289
It just felt very, very strange.

288
00:22:14,289 --> 00:22:15,289
Hey you.

289
00:22:15,289 --> 00:22:16,289
What is it?

290
00:22:16,289 --> 00:22:18,289
What's going on?

291
00:22:18,289 --> 00:22:19,289
When?

292
00:22:19,289 --> 00:22:21,289
The time to awaken has come.

293
00:22:21,289 --> 00:22:26,289
Nanachi, this is it.

294
00:22:26,289 --> 00:22:31,289
Starting now, it is no longer a dream.

295
00:23:30,034 --> 00:24:00,014
Thank you.

